  it is on the page. When that URL arrives, enable it in both files.

  ── WHY THIS IS ITS OWN ROOT, NOT SCOPED UNDER #umoya-footer ────
  The dialog is position: fixed, and a fixed element inside an
  ancestor carrying transform / filter / will-change is positioned
  against THAT ancestor instead of the viewport — which Elementor
  motion effects can introduce at any time. So, exactly like
  homepage-revamp/homepage-form-popup.html, this moves itself to
  document.body on init and therefore carries its own id and its own
  scoped CSS. The style block lives inside the element, so it travels
  with it.

  ⚠ NEVER WRITE A LITERAL style OR script TAG INSIDE A COMMENT IN
  THIS FILE. The live site minifies inline CSS BEFORE it strips HTML
  comments, and it finds style blocks by regex. A mention of that tag
  in a comment therefore opens a "stylesheet" that only closes at the
  next real closing tag — swallowing the comment's own terminator.
  The comment then runs on to the NEXT terminator further down the
  file and takes every element in between with it.

  This is not hypothetical: it silently deleted this popup's opening
  div, its entire stylesheet, the dialog wrapper, the close button,
  the eyebrow, the heading and the rule on the live site, leaving the
  body copy stranded and unstyled at the foot of every page. Write
  "style block" or "the script", never the tag itself.

  BRAND: font-family: inherit; palette tokens only. ES5 IIFE.
  WCAG AA (44px close target, focus trap, Esc, restored focus).
=================================================================
-->
